// Status codes returned by std.tls through its integer error channel. They
// form one SultanC-defined range (-2000 and below) that does not overlap the
// negative OS statuses produced by std.net, so callers can tell a TLS
// failure from a socket failure. A fatal alert received from the peer is
// reported as -3000 - AlertDescription (RFC 8446 6.2).

